# The licence list is **data, not source**: each notice is a byte length followed by
# exactly that many bytes, so a checkout that rewrote its line endings would move every
# entry's text off its own length and the file would read as no notices at all. That is
# what it did on Windows, silently, until a test said four hundred packages do not fit in
# zero notices. It must arrive exactly as `scripts/gen_licenses.py` wrote it.
crates/frus-demo/assets/licenses.txt -text

# Said rather than detected: a golden that a checkout touched is a golden that fails for a
# reason nobody would look for in the rasteriser.
*.png binary
*.ttf binary
*.otf binary
*.dex binary
